  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Core Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the core architecture for this Smart Medical App Ecosystem. The immediate priority is the \"Role Switcher & Ecosystem Modules (Multi-Role Portal).\" I\'m outlining the specific features for the \"Patient/General User View,\" with a focus on Emergency SOS and live ambulance dispatch features, including the crucial need for instant one-tap SOS and real-time GPS map integration.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now expanding the feature set for the Smart Medical App Ecosystem. This includes tracking with ETA, driver contacts, nearby ER triage, and automated hospital alerts. The AI Health Suite is taking shape with Symptom Assessment, Disease Risk Calculators, and an AI Chatbot. I\'m also developing the Live Bed Availability Portal, Medicine Manager, Digital Health Record Vault, and Doctor Appointments & Telemedicine features.\n\n\n**Developing Additional Portals**\n\nI\'m developing the in-person slot feature, live video consultation simulator, and e-Prescriptions view now. I\'m building out a Blood Bank & Organ Donation Portal with real-time blood group availability. The Doctor Portal will include a patient queue, e-Prescription creator, and Smart Digital Referral Creator. I\'m also planning the Hospital Admin Portal, and developing an Ambulance Driver Portal.\n\n\n**Defining Additional Portals**\n\nI\'m now deep diving into the functionality of specialized portals. The Ambulance Driver Portal will involve GPS-based route simulation for emergency callouts, including patient drop-off and real-time vital updates. The Lab Staff Portal is next, where test order management, and lab report uploads (with AI-powered data extraction) will be key. The Pharmacy/Blood Bank Staff Portal will feature medicine inventory and emergency blood stock management. Finally, the Super Admin Dashboard will provide system-wide statistics, audit logs, and overall control.\n\n**Building Server API Routes**\n\nI am now focusing on the server-side architecture. I\'m actively defining express API routes in `server.ts`, including a healthcheck endpoint and an AI-powered symptom checker using Gemini. I\'m structuring responses with JSON and prioritizing clear schemas. The API will also be ready to handle Red Flags, which will immediately trigger an escalation or warning.\n\n\n**Organizing API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now organizing and defining specific API endpoints. I am focused on structuring the `/api/ai` endpoints. This involves using Gemini to calculate disease risks based on metrics, create a smart referral engine, and extract medication details from images. I am planning the `/api/hospitals`, `/api/ambulances`, `/api/referrals`, and `/api/blood-bank` routes, to handle key functions.\n\n\n**Defining Project Data**\n\nI am now structuring the data definitions and initial mock data within `src/`. I\'ve created detailed TypeScript interfaces in `src/types.ts` for all the core entities, including users, patients, doctors, and all the relevant data points. Initial rich mock datasets for several entities are stored in `src/data/mockData.ts`. Further, I\'ve designed the foundational UI components with `Navbar.tsx` and `PatientDashboard.tsx`. I am also working on the `EmergencySOSModal.tsx` for real-time SOS dispatching.\n\n\n**Developing Patient-Focused Components**\n\nI\'m now deep into designing the patient-focused UI components. I\'ve built interactive tools like `SymptomChecker.tsx` for AI symptom assessment with a body selector, a comprehensive `RiskPrediction.tsx` for AI health risk prediction and score charts, and a Gemini-powered `AIChatbot.tsx`. There is also a `BedAvailability.tsx` module for real-time bed-finding with filterable attributes. I\'m working on a `MedicineManager.tsx`, and a `HealthRecordsVault.tsx`. I\'ve started the `DoctorConsultation.tsx` which will allow a user to book consultations. Also built is a `BloodAndOrganPortal.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 72034497
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
