    thinking: "**Structuring Frontend Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on modular frontend component creation. I\'m building out the directory structure, starting with the `src/components/` directory. I\'m planning out the subcomponents, including `Navbar.tsx` which will handle navigation with the role switcher, notifications, SOS trigger, and profile badge. Also, I will organize the `ReferralWorkflow`.\n\n\n**Defining Patient Components**\n\nI\'ve transitioned to patient-centric components. I\'m fleshing out `PatientDashboard.tsx` with modules for health scores, vitals, SOS triggers, medication alarms, bed search, AI diagnostics, and ABHA ID integration. Also I am implementing a dynamic emergency SOS modal and an AI symptom checker, including a risk assessment tool utilizing Gemini AI for detailed health analysis.\n\n\n**Expanding Patient-Focused Modules**\n\nI\'m now integrating more patient features. I\'m developing an AI-driven chatbot (`AIChatbot.tsx`) and a live bed search component (`BedAvailability.tsx`). Furthermore, I\'m working on a medicine manager with OCR scanning and a health records vault incorporating ABHA card and lab report interpretation. I\'m also planning doctor consultation modules and a blood and organ portal for improved patient care.\n\n\n"
